((
Morse trainer
-------------

In order to train my ears for Morse characters and words, I want to build
a "bug" type of Morse key, with a single blade in the center and two contact
points, one on each side, one for dits and one for dahs. 

The key then handles timing, in that as long as a contact is closed, it
repeats dits or dahs at correct length and inbetween space, as well as 
inbetween symbol time (one dit long).

This eliminates the issue of "button bounce", both because I will not use
buttons, but just contact points, so no springs involved, but also because
once detecting a contact on one of the points, it will generate the symbol,
and space following it, before checking the points again.

I also want to display the characters on an LCD display (I2C), and implement
a simple menu system for setting the speed. 
))


((
The position is calcualated as follows: 
- start with 1
- for a dit, left shift one
- for a dah, left shift one and add 1

After playing a sound (dit or dah), we reset timer 0, and in the
main check if more than 3 ticks has elapsed, which indicates 
next letter, so we show the letter associated with the current code
))

: Chars
	s" __ETIANMSURWDKGOHVF_L_PJBXCYZQ__54_3___2__+____16=/___(_7___8_90____________?________.____@______-___________)_____,"
;

: Len Chars c@ ;
: Char (pos -- char) Chars + 1+ c@ ;

(-- pins --)
13 constant LED
6 constant BUZZ  (-- must support PWM --)
7 constant DIT
5 constant DAH

60 constant Tick  (-- length of dit at 20 wpm --)

: In (pin) IN Pins .setIn ;
: Out (pin) IN Pins .setOut ;
: Dr (pin) IN Pins .readDigital ;
: Dw (value pin) IN Pins .writeDigital ;
: Aw (value pin) IN Pins .writeAnalog ;


: Init
	DIT In
	DAH In
	LED Out
	BUZZ Out
;


: On  
	1 LED Dw 
	60 BUZZ Aw ;
: Off 
	0 LED Dw 
	0 BUZZ Dw ;


(-- check if contacts closed --)
: Dit? (--bool) 0 DIT Dr not ret? 1+ ;
: Dah? (--bool) 0 DAH Dr not ret? 1+ ;

(-- reset timer 0 --)
: TZero 0 IN Timers .set ;

(-- play dit or dah, followed by a one dit delay before returning --)
: Play (ticks) 
	On Tick * delay 
	Off
	TZero
	(-- enforce at least 1 tick delay --)
	Tick delay ;

: Test
	Init
	/1
		key? ret?
		1 Play
		3 Play
		1 Play
		2 Tick * delay 

		1 Play
		2 Tick * delay

		1 Play
		1 Play
		1 Play
		2 Tick * delay
		
		3 Play
		2 Tick * delay
	&1 jmp
;


(-- get timer 0 millis --)
: CSep? 0 IN Timers .get Tick 3 * > ;

(-- check for symbols (dit/dah), play, and update code --)
: Sym (code--code) 
	Dit? if 
		1 Play
		1 << 
	else
		Dah? if
			3 Play
			1 << 1+
		then
	then
;

(-- look up character from code, show it, return 1 as new code --)
: Show (code -- 1)
	dup 1 == &1 jmp?
	dup Len >= &1 jmp?
	Char emit
	1 ret
	
	/1 drop 1
;
		
(-- Loop forever, and if character separation pause, show character --) 
: Main
	Init
	1 (--current code--)
	/1 
		key? ret?
		Sym   (code)
		CSep? if Show then (code)
		&1 jmp
;

